Both shipped in 0700229:

**One form everywhere.** The sentence spelling no longer exists — `a_source_file_stays_under_the_line_budget` *is* the check, in every position: the getter name, the `[…]` label in findings, the `"check"` field in `ivue-standards-skip.json`, the severities key, and the `--prove` argument. Grep one string, you've found every site; replace it, you've renamed the check completely. And it's not just convention — `prove()` now refuses any check whose name isn't its own getter (`the name is not its getter — one snake_case form is the whole identity`), and the constitution test asserts `GateClass[check.name].name === check.name` for all 38, so drift between forms is structurally impossible.

**The severity menu.** `severities` now admits an explicit `'error'` (validated but a no-op), and `house-gate.ts` ships the complete 39-entry menu:

```ts
static get severities(): Readonly<Record<string, 'error' | 'warn' | 'off'>> {
  return {
    exactly_one_reactive_source_is_installed: 'error',
    a_public_class_publishes_its_namespace_manifest: 'error',
    …all 39…
    a_source_file_stays_under_the_line_budget: 'error',
  };
}
```

So the example gate blocks exactly what the base gate blocks — but every ruling a team could make is already a visible line waiting to be flipped to `'warn'` or `'off'`, which is precisely the shape an agent edits well. Verified: base prove 48/42/0, house prove 49/43/0 (identity rule passing on all 39), newsletter baseline unchanged, constitution 6/6, tsc clean. Born-red was witnessed on the spec before the rename landed.

